{"availability":"available","full":"csharikrishna/panelprobe","name":"panelprobe","description":"Pixel-perfect display test patterns in your browser — OLED true black, dead pixels, motion clarity, gamma, banding & touch. Free, open source, no tracking.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-12T15:22:41Z","updated":"2026-09-13T07:27:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://csharikrishna.github.io/panelprobe/","topics":["backlight-bleed","calibration","dead-pixel","display-test","gamma","github-pages","html5-canvas","monitor-test","motion-blur","oled","screen-test","vanilla-javascript"],"demo":"https://csharikrishna.github.io/panelprobe/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:09:44.932Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T07:09:44.932Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T07:09:44.932Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.482Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T07:25:54.678Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T07:09:44.932Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Display test patterns and calibration aids for OLED, IPS, and mobile screens, running entirely in your browser.","Test videos are compressed. Codecs smear near-black detail and add banding and blocking, which are exactly the artifacts you're trying to spot. PanelProbe draws every pattern losslessly to a canvas mapped 1:1 to your device pixels. There's nothing to install and nothing leaves your machine."],"features":["26 test patterns in five categories, each with a one-key shortcut.","Test All steps through the 24 non-strobe tests automatically — 10 seconds each, with pause and skip.","Guided Wizard walks you through nine pass/issue checks. It produces a report you can print or save as PDF, or export as JSON, with advice for each issue.","True 1:1 pixel mapping. The canvas backing store follows the device-pixel content box, so it stays exact even at fractional scaling (